From 99db55071ad8c4ac02fcdd65eb159abe68b4ae37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Berkay Dokuyucu <berkaydokuyucu05@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:43:06 +0300
Subject: Apple Silicon performance fork: fast depth, Vulkan via MoltenVK, TCG
 tuning

Graphics:
- Fast depth option (default on): fixed-function depth and polygon offset
  instead of geometry-shader depth, consistent across all primitives
- Quads/quad strips drawn as indexed triangles instead of geometry shaders
- Vulkan renderer on macOS via MoltenVK: optional geometry shaders,
  IOSurface display interop with the GL UI, portability extensions
- GL capability cache, uniform dirty tracking (GL and Vulkan), GL fences
  for display hand-off, skip rendering while the window is hidden

CPU emulation:
- Sleep in guest polling loops (store-free self loops) until devices make
  progress or the vCPU is kicked
- Halt in the Xbox kernel idle loop
- NEON fast path for packed single-precision add/sub/mul
- Softfloat hardfloat fix for exact zero results, larger TB jump cache,
  fewer MAP_JIT write-protect toggles

macOS: USER_INTERACTIVE QoS for emulation threads, kqueue NOTE_CRITICAL
timers, audio workers sized to performance cores, -O3/ThinLTO with
-mcpu=apple-m1 by default.

Diagnostics (env-gated): XEMU_PERF_LOG, XEMU_TCG_STATS, XEMU_AUTO_SCREENSHOT.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
