diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 776bbfa45c..9ee89f8436 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1 +1,139 @@
+# xemu for Apple Silicon (unofficial performance fork)
+
+An **unofficial** fork of [xemu](https://xemu.app), the original Xbox emulator,
+tuned for Apple Silicon Macs (M1, M2, M3, M4, M5), especially fanless MacBook
+Airs. It focuses on reaching full speed and using less battery.
+
+> This is not an official xemu release and is not affiliated with the xemu
+> project. Bugs found in this build should be reported here, not upstream.
+
+## Results
+
+Measured on a **MacBook Air M4** (macOS 26, 60 Hz display, VSync on), using the
+*Crash Twinsanity* title screen and intro. CPU figures are host cores in use, sampled with
+macOS `sample` and `ps`.
+
+### Frame rate
+
+| Build | FPS |
+|---|---|
+| Upstream xemu 0.8 (precise depth through geometry shaders) | **18.3** |
+| This fork | **60** (VSync locked) |
+
+On Apple's OpenGL, geometry shaders are emulated by the driver. Upstream
+v0.8.x sends every triangle through one for depth precision, which is why
+v0.8 can be unplayable on Macs that ran v0.7 fine.
+
+### CPU use at 60 FPS (normal power mode)
+
+| Step | Process CPU | Emulated CPU thread |
+|---|---|---|
+| Timer, JIT and audio fixes | 1.30 cores | 97% |
+| + Xbox kernel idle loop halts instead of spinning | 0.97 | 42% |
+| + float, uniform cache, NEON SSE, bigger jump cache | **0.90** | **32%** |
+
+Main emulation loop exits: **67 million/s → 73 thousand/s**. Jump cache
+misses: **680k/s → 287k/s**. Time spent in software float: **−49%**.
+
+### CPU use at 60 FPS (battery, Low Power Mode)
+
+| | Before | After |
+|---|---|---|
+| Whole process | 1.36 cores | **1.10 cores** (0.80 average over 3 min) |
+| Emulated CPU thread | 81% | **38%** |
+| GPU thread, OpenGL | 39.5% | **32%** |
+| GPU thread, Vulkan (new on macOS) | — | **18–22%** |
+
+Less CPU means a cooler MacBook Air, longer battery life, and more headroom
+before the chip has to throttle.
+
+## What changed
+
+**Graphics (NV2A)**
+- **Fast depth** (Settings → Display → *Fast depth*, on by default). Uses
+  fixed-function depth plus polygon offset instead of geometry-shader
+  depth. Every primitive uses the same depth path, so multi-pass effects don't
+  z-fight or flicker. Early-Z and hidden-surface removal stay enabled on Apple's
+  tile-based GPUs.
+- **Quads become indexed triangles**, so HUDs, text, sprites and particles
+  skip the geometry shader entirely.
+- **Vulkan renderer on macOS** through MoltenVK (bundled). It works without
+  geometry shaders, and frames reach the UI with no copy through an IOSurface
+  shared with OpenGL. Its GPU thread uses about 30% less CPU than OpenGL.
+- OpenGL state cache (no redundant `glEnable`/`glDisable` calls), shader uniform
+  dirty tracking, and GPU fences instead of `glFinish` for display hand-off.
+- Rendering stops while the window is hidden or minimized.
+
+**CPU emulation (TCG, x86 → arm64)**
+- **Polling-loop sleep**: games spin on memory the GPU writes, for example the
+  Direct3D push-buffer fence wait. The translator detects these store-free loops
+  and they sleep until the emulated GPU makes progress or an interrupt arrives.
+  This cut emulated CPU time roughly in half in GPU-bound scenes.
+- **Idle loop halt**: the Xbox kernel's idle loop halts the virtual CPU
+  until the next interrupt.
+- **NEON packed SSE**: `addps`, `subps` and `mulps` run as one ARM vector instruction. Results and
+  exception flags match QEMU's softfloat bit for bit (6.2 million test vectors).
+- Fixed the softfloat hardware-float fast path rejecting exact-zero results (24
+  million test cases verified), and enlarged the jump cache to 16K entries.
+- Fewer redundant MAP_JIT write-protect toggles.
+
+**macOS integration**
+- Emulation threads run at the `USER_INTERACTIVE` QoS class (performance cores).
+- Precise kqueue `NOTE_CRITICAL` timers: about 12 µs late, versus about 110 µs for `nanosleep`.
+- Audio voice workers are sized to the Mac's number of performance cores.
+- Builds with `-O3`, ThinLTO and `-mcpu=apple-m1`, so one binary runs on every
+  M-series chip. `-ffast-math` is deliberately not used, because guest floats need IEEE
+  semantics.
+
+## Install
+
+1. Download `xemu-apple-silicon.zip` from
+   [Releases](../../releases), unzip it, and move `xemu.app` to Applications.
+2. The app is ad-hoc signed, not notarized, so remove the quarantine flag
+   once:
+   ```sh
+   xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/xemu.app
+   ```
+3. Provide your own MCPX boot ROM, BIOS and HDD image as with upstream xemu
+   (see the [xemu setup guide](https://xemu.app/docs/required-files/)). None
+   are included.
+
+Requires an Apple Silicon Mac running macOS 14 Sonoma or later. Intel Macs are not supported.
+
+**Tips**
+- Keep *Fast depth* on. Turn it off only if a game shows depth artifacts. It is
+  then much slower on Macs, as in upstream.
+- Try *Renderer → Vulkan* for lower CPU use. OpenGL stays the default because
+  it has had more testing.
+
+## Known limitations
+
+- Most testing so far has been on one game's title screen and intro on an M4.
+  Real gameplay across many titles still needs testing; reports are welcome.
+- Fast depth can cause depth artifacts in a few games that rely on exact NV2A depth precision.
+- Vulkan on macOS has no wide lines or logic ops, and flat-shaded geometry
+  that uses the "last vertex" convention may show wrong colors.
+- Not checked on M1, M2, M3 or M5 hardware yet. The binary targets the baseline M1 instruction set.
+
+## Building
+
+```sh
+brew install ninja pkgconf meson molten-vk vulkan-headers dylibbundler
+./build.sh                      # portable build (-mcpu=apple-m1)
+XEMU_MCPU=native ./build.sh     # tuned for your own chip only
+```
+
+Debug aids (environment variables):
+- `XEMU_PERF_LOG=1` prints FPS and renderer counters every second.
+- `XEMU_TCG_STATS=1` (or `=prof`) prints CPU-emulator statistics and finds hot guest loops.
+- `XEMU_AUTO_SCREENSHOT=<seconds>` saves one screenshot after that many seconds.
+
+## License
+
+xemu is GPL-2.0 (see [LICENSE](LICENSE)); this fork is under the same license.
+The bundled MoltenVK is Apache-2.0. All credit for xemu goes to the xemu
+project and its contributors.
+
+---
+
 Please visit [https://xemu.app](https://xemu.app) for more information.
diff --git a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
index d93cd1734d..1433c0df5a 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
@@ -953,21 +953,316 @@ static inline void cpu_loop_exec_tb(CPUState *cpu, TranslationBlock *tb,
 
 /* main execution loop */
 
+/*
+ * XEMU_TCG_STATS diagnostics: per second, count main loop iterations and why
+ * execution left translated code, plus the guest PCs most often resumed at
+ * after an unchainable exit (with surrounding code bytes).
+ */
+#define TCG_STATS_SLOTS 1024
+static struct {
+    int enabled;
+    int64_t ts;
+    uint64_t iters, gen, null_exit, add_jump, page2, irq, exc;
+    struct { vaddr pc; uint32_t count; } pcs[TCG_STATS_SLOTS];
+} tcg_stats = { .enabled = -1 };
+
+static void tcg_stats_record_pc(vaddr pc)
+{
+    unsigned h = (pc * 0x9E3779B1u) % TCG_STATS_SLOTS;
+    for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
+        unsigned j = (h + i) % TCG_STATS_SLOTS;
+        if (tcg_stats.pcs[j].pc == pc || !tcg_stats.pcs[j].count) {
+            tcg_stats.pcs[j].pc = pc;
+            tcg_stats.pcs[j].count++;
+            return;
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__aarch64__)
+/*
+ * With XEMU_TCG_STATS=prof, sample the host PC of the vCPU thread on SIGPROF
+ * to find guest code that loops inside chained translated code, which never
+ * shows up as a main loop iteration.
+ */
+#include <signal.h>
+#include <sys/time.h>
+#include <sys/ucontext.h>
+#include <dlfcn.h>
+#include "system/memory.h"
+#define TCG_PROF_SLOTS 4096
+static uintptr_t tcg_prof_pcs[TCG_PROF_SLOTS];
+static uint32_t tcg_prof_regs[TCG_PROF_SLOTS][8];
+static unsigned tcg_prof_n;
+static pthread_t tcg_prof_thread;
+
+static void tcg_prof_handler(int sig, siginfo_t *info, void *uc_)
+{
+    ucontext_t *uc = uc_;
+    if (!pthread_equal(pthread_self(), tcg_prof_thread)) {
+        return;
+    }
+    unsigned n = qatomic_read(&tcg_prof_n);
+    if (n < TCG_PROF_SLOTS) {
+        tcg_prof_pcs[n] = uc->uc_mcontext->__ss.__pc;
+        if (current_cpu) {
+            CPUArchState *env = cpu_env(current_cpu);
+            for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
+                tcg_prof_regs[n][i] = ((uint32_t *)env)[i]; /* i386: regs[] first */
+            }
+        }
+        qatomic_set(&tcg_prof_n, n + 1);
+    }
+}
+
+static void *tcg_prof_kicker(void *opaque)
+{
+    for (;;) {
+        g_usleep(1000);
+        pthread_kill(tcg_prof_thread, SIGPROF);
+    }
+    return NULL;
+}
+
+static void tcg_prof_start(void)
+{
+    struct sigaction sa = { .sa_sigaction = tcg_prof_handler,
+                            .sa_flags = SA_SIGINFO | SA_RESTART };
+    sigset_t set;
+    pthread_t kicker;
+
+    tcg_prof_thread = pthread_self();
+    sigaction(SIGPROF, &sa, NULL);
+    sigemptyset(&set);
+    sigaddset(&set, SIGPROF);
+    pthread_sigmask(SIG_UNBLOCK, &set, NULL);
+    pthread_create(&kicker, NULL, tcg_prof_kicker, NULL);
+}
+
+static int tcg_prof_cmp(const void *a, const void *b)
+{
+    const TranslationBlock *x = *(TranslationBlock * const *)a;
+    const TranslationBlock *y = *(TranslationBlock * const *)b;
+    return x < y ? -1 : x > y;
+}
+
+static void tcg_prof_report(CPUState *cpu)
+{
+    unsigned n = qatomic_read(&tcg_prof_n);
+    TranslationBlock *tbs[TCG_PROF_SLOTS];
+    unsigned in_jit = 0;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+        tbs[i] = tcg_tb_lookup(tcg_prof_pcs[i]);
+        in_jit += tbs[i] != NULL;
+    }
+    /* Group samples outside translation blocks by host symbol */
+    {
+        struct { const char *sym; unsigned count; } syms[64];
+        int nsyms = 0;
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+            if (tbs[i]) {
+                continue;
+            }
+            Dl_info dli;
+            const char *sym = "?";
+            if (dladdr((void *)tcg_prof_pcs[i], &dli) && dli.dli_sname) {
+                sym = dli.dli_sname;
+            } else if (in_code_gen_buffer((void *)tcg_prof_pcs[i])) {
+                sym = "<jit, no tb>";
+            }
+            int k;
+            for (k = 0; k < nsyms && strcmp(syms[k].sym, sym); k++) {
+            }
+            if (k == nsyms && nsyms < ARRAY_SIZE(syms)) {
+                syms[nsyms].sym = sym;
+                syms[nsyms++].count = 0;
+            }
+            if (k < nsyms) {
+                syms[k].count++;
+            }
+        }
+        for (int t = 0; t < 12; t++) {
+            int best = -1;
+            for (int k = 0; k < nsyms; k++) {
+                if (syms[k].count && (best < 0 || syms[k].count > syms[best].count)) {
+                    best = k;
+                }
+            }
+            if (best < 0) {
+                break;
+            }
+            fprintf(stderr, "tcgprof:   host %4.1f%% %s\n",
+                    syms[best].count * 100.0 / n, syms[best].sym);
+            syms[best].count = 0;
+        }
+    }
+    /* Hottest raw host PCs, with their TB if any */
+    {
+        uintptr_t pcs[TCG_PROF_SLOTS];
+        memcpy(pcs, tcg_prof_pcs, n * sizeof(pcs[0]));
+        qsort(pcs, n, sizeof(pcs[0]), tcg_prof_cmp);
+        for (int t = 0; t < 4; t++) {
+            uintptr_t bestpc = 0;
+            unsigned bestc = 0;
+            for (unsigned i = 0; i < n;) {
+                unsigned j = i;
+                while (j < n && pcs[j] == pcs[i]) {
+                    j++;
+                }
+                if (pcs[i] && j - i > bestc) {
+                    bestc = j - i;
+                    bestpc = pcs[i];
+                }
+                i = j;
+            }
+            if (!bestc) {
+                break;
+            }
+            TranslationBlock *tb = tcg_tb_lookup(bestpc);
+            fprintf(stderr, "tcgprof:   hostpc %lx %4.1f%% tb=%p jit=%d\n",
+                    (unsigned long)bestpc, bestc * 100.0 / n, tb,
+                    in_code_gen_buffer((void *)bestpc));
+            for (unsigned i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+                if (pcs[i] == bestpc) {
+                    pcs[i] = 0;
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    qsort(tbs, n, sizeof(tbs[0]), tcg_prof_cmp);
+    fprintf(stderr, "tcgprof: %u samples, %u in translated code\n", n, in_jit);
+    for (int k = 0; k < 6; k++) {
+        TranslationBlock *best = NULL;
+        unsigned best_count = 0;
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < n;) {
+            unsigned j = i;
+            while (j < n && tbs[j] == tbs[i]) {
+                j++;
+            }
+            if (tbs[i] && j - i > best_count) {
+                best = tbs[i];
+                best_count = j - i;
+            }
+            i = j;
+        }
+        if (!best) {
+            break;
+        }
+        uint8_t code[48];
+        tb_page_addr_t phys = tb_page_addr0(best);
+        fprintf(stderr, "tcgprof:   %4.1f%% tb phys=%08" PRIx64 " size=%u icount=%u flags=%x bytes=",
+                best_count * 100.0 / n, (uint64_t)phys, best->size,
+                tb_cflags(best) & CF_COUNT_MASK, best->flags);
+        memcpy(code, qemu_map_ram_ptr(NULL, phys), MIN(sizeof(code), best->size));
+        for (int i = 0; i < (int)MIN(sizeof(code), best->size); i++) {
+            fprintf(stderr, "%02x", code[i]);
+        }
+        fprintf(stderr, "\n");
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+            if (tcg_tb_lookup(tcg_prof_pcs[i]) == best) {
+                uint32_t *rg = tcg_prof_regs[i];
+                uint32_t mem = 0;
+                cpu_memory_rw_debug(cpu, rg[2], &mem, 4, false);
+                fprintf(stderr, "tcgprof:     eax=%08x ecx=%08x edx=%08x ebx=%08x esp=%08x ebp=%08x esi=%08x edi=%08x [edx]=%08x\n",
+                        rg[0], rg[1], rg[2], rg[3], rg[4], rg[5], rg[6], rg[7], mem);
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+            if (tbs[i] == best) {
+                tbs[i] = NULL;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    qatomic_set(&tcg_prof_n, 0);
+}
+#else
+static void tcg_prof_start(void) {}
+static void tcg_prof_report(CPUState *cpu) {}
+#endif
+
+static void tcg_stats_report(CPUState *cpu)
+{
+    int64_t now = qemu_clock_get_us(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME);
+    double secs = (now - tcg_stats.ts) / 1e6;
+    if (secs < 1.0) {
+        return;
+    }
+    tcg_prof_report(cpu);
+    fprintf(stderr, "tcg: iters=%.0f/s gen=%.0f/s null_exit=%.0f/s "
+            "add_jump=%.0f/s page2=%.0f/s irq=%.0f/s exc=%.0f/s\n",
+            tcg_stats.iters / secs, tcg_stats.gen / secs,
+            tcg_stats.null_exit / secs, tcg_stats.add_jump / secs,
+            tcg_stats.page2 / secs, tcg_stats.irq / secs,
+            tcg_stats.exc / secs);
+    for (int n = 0; n < 6; n++) {
+        int best = -1;
+        for (int i = 0; i < TCG_STATS_SLOTS; i++) {
+            if (tcg_stats.pcs[i].count &&
+                (best < 0 || tcg_stats.pcs[i].count > tcg_stats.pcs[best].count)) {
+                best = i;
+            }
+        }
+        if (best < 0) {
+            break;
+        }
+        uint8_t code[32];
+        vaddr pc = tcg_stats.pcs[best].pc;
+        fprintf(stderr, "tcg:   resume pc=%08" VADDR_PRIx " %.0f/s bytes[-24..+8]=",
+                pc, tcg_stats.pcs[best].count / secs);
+        if (cpu_memory_rw_debug(cpu, pc - 24, code, sizeof(code), false) == 0) {
+            for (int i = 0; i < (int)sizeof(code); i++) {
+                fprintf(stderr, "%02x", code[i]);
+            }
+        }
+        fprintf(stderr, "\n");
+        tcg_stats.pcs[best].count = 0;
+    }
+    memset(tcg_stats.pcs, 0, sizeof(tcg_stats.pcs));
+    tcg_stats.iters = tcg_stats.gen = tcg_stats.null_exit = 0;
+    tcg_stats.add_jump = tcg_stats.page2 = tcg_stats.irq = tcg_stats.exc = 0;
+    tcg_stats.ts = now;
+}
+
 static int __attribute__((noinline))
 cpu_exec_loop(CPUState *cpu, SyncClocks *sc)
 {
     int ret;
 
+    if (tcg_stats.enabled < 0) {
+        const char *env = getenv("XEMU_TCG_STATS");
+        tcg_stats.enabled = env != NULL;
+        tcg_stats.ts = qemu_clock_get_us(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME);
+        if (env && !strcmp(env, "prof")) {
+            tcg_prof_start();
+        }
+    }
+
     /* if an exception is pending, we execute it here */
     while (!cpu_handle_exception(cpu, &ret)) {
         TranslationBlock *last_tb = NULL;
         int tb_exit = 0;
+        bool stats = tcg_stats.enabled;
+        bool prev_null_exit = false;
+
+        if (stats) {
